7262","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13697262"]},"doi":"10.1016/j.xpro.2026.104904","title":"Protocol for eVLP-mediated CRISPR-Cas9 and prime editing in pancreatic cancer cell lines.","authorString":"Timmins-Young C, Cordani M, Giovannetti E, Aslanoglou D, Gutierrez A, Costello E, Glenn M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Timmins-Young C","lastName":"Timmins-Young","firstName":"Chloe","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Liverpool Experimental Cancer Medicine Centre, University of Liverpool, Liverpool L69 3GE, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Cordani M","lastName":"Cordani","firstName":"Marco","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9342-4862"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Faculty of Biological Sciences, Complutense University of Madrid, Madrid, Spain; San Carlos Health Research Institute (IdISSC), 28040 Madrid, Spain."}]}},{"fullName":"Giovannetti E","lastName":"Giovannetti","firstName":"Elisa","initials":"E","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7565-7504"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Medical Oncology, Cancer Center Amsterdam, Amsterdam University Medical Center, Vrije Universiteit, Amsterdam, the Netherlands; Cancer Pharmacology Lab, Fondazione Pisana per La Scienza, Pisa, San Giuliano Terme, Italy."}]}},{"fullName":"Aslanoglou D","lastName":"Aslanoglou","firstName":"Despoina","initials":"D","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Medicine, Pharmacy and Biomedical Sciences, University of Portsmouth, Portsmouth, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Gutierrez A","lastName":"Gutierrez","firstName":"Alvaro","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Faculty of Pharmacy, Complutense University of Madrid, Madrid, Spain; San Carlos Health Research Institute (IdISSC), 28040 Madrid, Spain."}]}},{"fullName":"Costello E","lastName":"Costello","firstName":"Eithne","initials":"E","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Liverpool Experimental Cancer Medicine Centre, University of Liverpool, Liverpool L69 3GE, UK. Electronic address: ecostell@liverpool.ac.uk."}]}},{"fullName":"Glenn M","lastName":"Glenn","firstName":"Mark","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Liverpool Experimental Cancer Medicine Centre, University of Liverpool, Liverpool L69 3GE, UK. Electronic address: maglenn@liverpool.ac.uk."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9342-4862"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7565-7504"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"4","volume":"7","journalIssueId":4275788,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"STAR Protoc","title":"STAR protocols","essn":"2666-1667","issn":"2666-1667","isoabbreviation":"STAR Protoc","nlmid":"101769501"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-10-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"104904","abstractText":"Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) cell lines resist transfection, limiting gene-editing experiments. Here, we present a protocol for delivering CRISPR-Cas9 or prime editors into PDAC cell lines using retrovirus-derived engineered virus-like particles (eVLPs). We describe steps for generating eVLPs, packaging CRISPR-Cas9 ribonucleoproteins or prime editors with engineered prime-editing guide RNAs (epegRNAs), and transducing human PDAC cells. We use the HEK3 locus and NQO1 (NAD(P)H quinone dehydrogenase 1) exon 6 as example edits and controls, respectively. This protocol adapts readily to other genomic sites.","affiliation":"Liverpool Experimental Cancer Medicine Centre, University of Liverpool, Liverpool L69 3GE, UK.","publicationStatus":"aheadofprint","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Cancer","Crispr","Biotechnology And Bioengineering"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.xpro.2026.104904"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13697262"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13697262?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by-nc-nd","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["ensembl","doi"]},"dateOfCreation":"2026-10-18","dateOfRevision":"2026-10-28","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-10-17","firstPublicationDate":"2026-10-17","firstIndexDate":"2026-10-19","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-10-27","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42754893","source":"MED","pmid":"42754893","pmcid":"PMC13587479","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13587479"]},"doi":"10.1186/s13073-026-01772-1","title":"Accurate characterization of CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing outcomes and mosaicism with near-perfect long reads.","authorString":"Höijer I, van Schendel R, Emmanouilidou A, Östlund R, Bunikis I, Tijsterman M, den Hoed M, Ameur A.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Höijer I","lastName":"Höijer","firstName":"Ida","initials":"I","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3915-3384"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden. ida.hoijer@igp.uu.se."},{"affiliation":"SciLifeLab, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden. ida.hoijer@igp.uu.se."}]}},{"fullName":"van Schendel R","lastName":"van Schendel","firstName":"Robin","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Human Genetics, Leiden University Medical Center, Leiden, The Netherlands."}]}},{"fullName":"Emmanouilidou A","lastName":"Emmanouilidou","firstName":"Anastasia","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."},{"affiliation":"SciLifeLab, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Östlund R","lastName":"Östlund","firstName":"Rebecka","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."},{"affiliation":"SciLifeLab, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Bunikis I","lastName":"Bunikis","firstName":"Ignas","initials":"I","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."},{"affiliation":"SciLifeLab, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Tijsterman M","lastName":"Tijsterman","firstName":"Marcel","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Human Genetics, Leiden University Medical Center, Leiden, The Netherlands."}]}},{"fullName":"den Hoed M","lastName":"den Hoed","firstName":"Marcel","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."},{"affiliation":"SciLifeLab, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden."}]}},{"fullName":"Ameur A","lastName":"Ameur","firstName":"Adam","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6085-6749"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden. adam.ameur@igp.uu.se."},{"affiliation":"SciLifeLab, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden. adam.ameur@igp.uu.se."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6085-6749"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3915-3384"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"18","journalIssueId":4259383,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Genome Med","title":"Genome medicine","essn":"1756-994X","issn":"1756-994X","isoabbreviation":"Genome Med","nlmid":"101475844"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-09-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"135","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Genetic mosaicism is a well-recognized consequence of CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing, yet its characterization remains challenging, especially when it involves low-frequency structural variants. A comprehensive analysis of mosaicism requires deep and unbiased sequencing of the target loci, with accurate single-molecule reads.<h4>Methods</h4>We performed amplification-free PureTarget PacBio sequencing to investigate CRISPR-Cas9 outcomes at on-target and off-target sites in genome edited zebrafish and their offspring. CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing was performed by micro-injection in fertilized eggs at the single-cell stage.<h4>Results</h4>Thirty samples from pooled larvae and individual zebrafish were successfully sequenced, resulting in > 1100x average target coverage. The PacBio reads reached an exceptional accuracy (QV39) over the target regions, with every read originating from a unique DNA molecule. The two haplotypes of the target loci displayed a balanced depth of coverage, while long-range PCR of the same samples resulted in skewed data. Further analysis of the PureTarget data revealed widespread genetic mosaicism in individual founder (F0) fish, with up to 18 distinct on-target events and 11 off-target events present in a single adult founder. Several CRISPR-Cas9 editing outcomes, including large structural variants and off-target mutations, were inherited to the F1 generation. Notably, as many as seven unique editing events were found among sibling F1 juvenile offspring derived from a single founder pair, thereby confirming the presence of genetic mosaicism in germ cells of founder zebrafish. This implies that some consequences of CRISPR-Cas9 editing may emerge only in the second generation. We also analyzed DNA methylation signals in the PureTarget data but did not observe altered 5mC CpG levels in genome edited samples.<h4>Conclusions</h4>PureTarget enables efficient, accurate, and unbiased profiling of genetic mosaicism and DNA methylation at pre-defined genomic regions. Our results show that CRISPR-Cas9-induced mosaicism is widespread and represents an important factor to consider in genome editing experiments.","affiliation":"Department of Immunology, Genetics and Pathology, Uppsala University, Uppsala, Sweden. ida.hoijer@igp.uu.se.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Uppsala University","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Zebrafish","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Mosaicism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genome"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Editing","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Mosaicism","Structural Variation","Genome Editing","Single-molecule Sequencing","Targeted Sequencing","Crispr-cas9","Off-target Mutations","Long-read Sequencing","Puretarget"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13073-026-01772-1"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13587479"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13587479?pdf=render"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"source":"PPR","id":"PPR1080897","type":"Preprint in","note":"Link created based on a title-first author match","orderIn":10002}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":1,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["bioproject"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-09-18","dateOfCreation":"2026-09-18","dateOfRevision":"2026-09-20","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-09-15","firstPublicationDate":"2026-09-15","firstIndexDate":"2026-09-18","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-09-20","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42747567","source":"MED","pmid":"42747567","pmcid":"PMC13582722","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13582722"]},"doi":"10.1007/s00253-026-14030-6","title":"An inducer-independent, single-plasmid CRISPR-Cas9 system for genome editing in Bacillus species.","authorString":"Hilkmann M, Welsch N, Felle MF, Schweder T, Appelbaum M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Hilkmann M","lastName":"Hilkmann","firstName":"Maximilian","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Marine Biotechnology, 17489, Greifswald, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Welsch N","lastName":"Welsch","firstName":"Norma","initials":"N","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Marine Biotechnology, 17489, Greifswald, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Felle MF","lastName":"Felle","firstName":"Max Fabian","initials":"MF","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"BASF SE, 67063, Ludwigshafen Am Rhein, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Schweder T","lastName":"Schweder","firstName":"Thomas","initials":"T","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7213-3596"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany. schweder@uni-greifswald.de."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Marine Biotechnology, 17489, Greifswald, Germany. schweder@uni-greifswald.de."}]}},{"fullName":"Appelbaum M","lastName":"Appelbaum","firstName":"Mathis","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany. mathis.appelbaum@basf.com."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Marine Biotechnology, 17489, Greifswald, Germany. mathis.appelbaum@basf.com."},{"affiliation":"BASF SE, 67063, Ludwigshafen Am Rhein, Germany. mathis.appelbaum@basf.com."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7213-3596"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"110","journalIssueId":4261033,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Appl Microbiol Biotechnol","title":"Applied microbiology and biotechnology","essn":"1432-0614","issn":"0175-7598","isoabbreviation":"Appl Microbiol Biotechnol","nlmid":"8406612"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-09-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"278","abstractText":"Advances in molecular biology tools are essential for streamlining and accelerating genetic engineering of cells across industrial and academic applications. While CRISPR-Cas improves genome editing efficiency, current systems have limitations and are often host specific, which restricts their versatility. This study describes a versatile CRISPR-Cas9 system for genome editing in industrially relevant Bacillus species. By adapting the well-established pJOE8999 vector-based CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing system, we constructed an inducer-independent, broad-host-range genome editing system. It maintains the benefits of low toxicity to the target cell and the cloning host as well as the ease to use of a single-plasmid CRISPR-Cas9 system. We utilized the constitutive Sigma70-type promoter from the conserved veg gene of Bacillus, to develop and test the suitability of promoter variants of different strengths for Cas9 expression. Successful gene deletions in three different Bacillus species demonstrated the versatility of the modified system for this industrially important genus. This was further confirmed by the integration of a reporter gene fusion and the introduction of a single point mutation in the genome of Bacillus licheniformis. This one-step CRISPR-based transformation protocol developed in this study enables fast genome editing workflows with minimal hands-on time. KEY POINTS: • Editing and screening of promoter variants for balanced Cas9 expression in Bacillus. • Development of a versatile inducer-independent, single-plasmid CRISPR-Cas-based system. • Verification of the modified CRISPR-based system for genome editing in different Bacilli.","affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Universität Greifswald","orderIn":0},{"agency":"BASF","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Bacillus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Gene Deletion"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genome, Bacterial"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Plasmids","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Promoter Regions, Genetic"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Editing","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Bacillus","Promoter","Genome Editing","Crispr-cas","Strain Optimization"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00253-026-14030-6"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13582722"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13582722?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl"