, Amsterdam, Netherlands."}]}},{"fullName":"van Dam TJP","lastName":"van Dam","firstName":"Teunis J P","initials":"TJP","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8122-190X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Research, Sanquin Blood Supply Foundation, Amsterdam, Netherlands."},{"affiliation":"Landsteiner Laboratory, Amsterdam UMC, University of Amsterdam, Amsterdam, Netherlands."}]}},{"fullName":"Fagerholm SC","lastName":"Fagerholm","firstName":"Suzanna C","initials":"SC","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0354-8763"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Molecular and Integrative Biosciences, Faculty of Biological and Environmental Sciences, University of Helsinki, Helsinki, Finland."}]}},{"fullName":"Moser M","lastName":"Moser","firstName":"Markus","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8825-5566"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institute of Experimental Hematology School of Medicine and Health, Technical University of Munich , Munich, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Center for Translational Cancer Research (TranslaTUM), School of Medicine and Health, Technical University of Munich , Munich, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Kuijpers TW","lastName":"Kuijpers","firstName":"Taco W","initials":"TW","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7421-3370"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Research, Sanquin Blood Supply Foundation, Amsterdam, Netherlands."},{"affiliation":"Landsteiner Laboratory, Amsterdam UMC, University of Amsterdam, Amsterdam, Netherlands."},{"affiliation":"Department of Pediatric Immunology, Rheumatology & Infectious Diseases, Emma Children's Hospital, Amsterdam UMC, University of Amsterdam, Amsterdam, Netherlands."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7073-9677"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8825-5566"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0354-8763"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1676-0720"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2292-5982"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2645-1008"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7421-3370"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8122-190X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8227-1888"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9892-7271"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1064-0776"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2159-7224"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"6","volume":"2","journalIssueId":4249539,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Nov","monthOfPublication":11,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Hum Immun","title":"Journal of human immunity","essn":"3065-8993","issn":"3065-8993","isoabbreviation":"J Hum Immun","nlmid":"9919054337406676"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-11-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e20260086","abstractText":"Mutations in human FERMT3 (encoding kindlin-3 protein) impair β2 integrin activity in neutrophils from patients with leukocyte adhesion deficiency III (LAD-III). Yet kindlin-3's contribution to neutrophil integrin affinity regulation and function remains unclear. Using CD34+ human hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells (HSPCs) differentiated into neutrophils, we investigated how CRISPR/Cas9-mediated kindlin-3 deletion affects neutrophil characteristics. CRISPR/Cas9 targeting FERMT3 resulted in an ∼80-bp deletion within exon 2, impairing protein production. FERMT3 KO neutrophils retained normal in vitro development and phenotype with similar surface marker expression, nuclear morphology, and expansion potential compared with untreated cultured neutrophils. Loss of kindlin-3 abolished zymosan-induced NADPH oxidase activity, recapitulating the ROS production defect of LAD-III neutrophils. However, although basal adhesion was reduced, stimulus-induced integrin activity remained largely intact. FERMT3 KO neutrophils retained fMLP-driven chemotaxis while showing impaired migration in response to C5a. Together, these findings show that disruption of kindlin-3 largely recapitulates the LAD-III phenotype while exerting some effector functions upon stimulation without intact kindlin-3.","affiliation":"Department of Research, Sanquin Blood Supply Foundation, Amsterdam, Netherlands.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"E-Rare-3","grantId":"355527","orderIn":0},{"agency":"E-Rare-3","grantId":"JTC2018SF","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Dutch Ministry of Health","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Sanquin Blood Supply Product and Process Development Cellular Products Fund","orderIn":0},{"agency":"E-Rare-3","grantId":"326358","orderIn":0}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.70962/jhi.20260086"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13685712"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13685712?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["refseq"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-10-22","dateOfCreation":"2026-10-22","dateOfRevision":"2026-10-24","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-10-21","firstPublicationDate":"2026-10-21","firstIndexDate":"2026-10-23","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-10-24","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42601370","source":"MED","pmid":"42601370","pmcid":"PMC13476449","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13476449"]},"doi":"10.1038/s41598-026-61844-5","title":"Design and transfection of CRISPR/Cas9 constructs for the myostatin gene in Labeo rohita muscle cells.","authorString":"Iqbal G, Pinto N, Pawaskar D, Sonwane AA, Rasal KD, Singh LS, Chikkathimmashetty NN, Goswami M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Iqbal G","lastName":"Iqbal","firstName":"Gowhar","initials":"G","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Fish Genetics and Biotechnology, ICAR - Central Institute of Fisheries Education, Panch Marg, Yari Road, Mumbai, 400061, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Pinto N","lastName":"Pinto","firstName":"Nevil","initials":"N","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Fish Genetics and Biotechnology, ICAR - Central Institute of Fisheries Education, Panch Marg, Yari Road, Mumbai, 400061, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Pawaskar D","lastName":"Pawaskar","firstName":"Darshan","initials":"D","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Fish Genetics and Biotechnology, ICAR - Central Institute of Fisheries Education, Panch Marg, Yari Road, Mumbai, 400061, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Sonwane AA","lastName":"Sonwane","firstName":"Arvind A","initials":"AA","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Fish Genetics and Biotechnology, ICAR - Central Institute of Fisheries Education, Panch Marg, Yari Road, Mumbai, 400061, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Rasal KD","lastName":"Rasal","firstName":"Kiran D","initials":"KD","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Fish Genetics and Biotechnology, ICAR - Central Institute of Fisheries Education, Panch Marg, Yari Road, Mumbai, 400061, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Singh LS","lastName":"Singh","firstName":"Lukram Sushil","initials":"LS","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Fish Genetics and Biotechnology, ICAR - Central Institute of Fisheries Education, Panch Marg, Yari Road, Mumbai, 400061, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Chikkathimmashetty NN","lastName":"Chikkathimmashetty","firstName":"Nidarshan N","initials":"NN","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Fish Genetics and Biotechnology, ICAR - Central Institute of Fisheries Education, Panch Marg, Yari Road, Mumbai, 400061, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Goswami M","lastName":"Goswami","firstName":"Mukunda","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Fish Genetics and Biotechnology, ICAR - Central Institute of Fisheries Education, Panch Marg, Yari Road, Mumbai, 400061, India. mukugoswami@gmail.com."}]}}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"16","journalIssueId":4223254,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Sci Rep","title":"Scientific reports","essn":"2045-2322","issn":"2045-2322","isoabbreviation":"Sci Rep","nlmid":"101563288"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-07-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"25509","abstractText":"Myostatin (mstn) is a negative regulator of skeletal muscle growth and is considered as an important target for enhancing aquaculture production. The present study aimed to design and validate single-guide RNAs (sgRNAs) and CRISPR/Cas9 constructs for exon 1 of the mstnb gene in Labeo rohita, and to evaluate their transfection efficiency in the L. rohita dorsal muscle (LRDM) cell line at the 10th, 20th, and 30th passages. sgRNAs were designed and cloned into the pSpCas9(BB)-2A-GFP (PX458) vector using BbsI restriction digestion and ligation. Successful insertion and correct orientation of the sgRNAs were confirmed through Sanger sequencing. LRDM cells were revived and maintained in L-15 medium supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum. Transfection was performed at the 10th, 20th, and 30th passages. Distinct GFP-positive cells were observed at all passages for both sgRNA constructs, indicating the ability of the developed cell line to successfully express the constructs across different passages. The study successfully established CRISPR/Cas9 plasmid constructs for the mstnb gene in L. rohita and demonstrated their transfection in LRDM cell line across multiple passages. These findings provide a basis for future studies on genome editing approaches using CRISPR/Cas9 constructs in fish muscle cell lines and highlight the potential application of CRISPR/Cas9 technology for genetic engineering applications in fish muscle cells.","affiliation":"Division of Fish Genetics and Biotechnology, ICAR - Central Institute of Fisheries Education, Panch Marg, Yari Road, Mumbai, 400061, India.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Line"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Muscle Cells","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Cyprinidae","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Transfection","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Myostatin","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"RNA, Guide, CRISPR-Cas Systems","meshQuali