hypercholesterolemia, and cancer. The success of these therapies hinges on the effective delivery of CRISPR/Cas9 components to target regions, efficient Cas endonuclease editing, repair profiles generated, and their resulting outcomes. Here, we discuss the factors that influence the generation of CRISPR/Cas9-generated repair edits, the overall profiles, and outcome prediction(s), as well as the analytical tools that have been developed to date. Finally, how this technology has been used towards a functional HIV-1 cure is discussed.","affiliation":"Department of Microbiology and Immunology, Drexel University College of Medicine, Philadelphia, PA 19102, USA.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIMH NIH HHS","acronym":"MH","grantId":"R01 MH110360","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIMH NIH HHS","acronym":"MH","grantId":"MH079785","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIMH NIH HHS","acronym":"MH","grantId":"P30 MH092177","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIMH NIH HHS","acronym":"MH","grantId":"MH092177","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIMH NIH HHS","acronym":"MH","grantId":"T32 MH079785","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIMH NIH HHS","acronym":"MH","grantId":"MH110360","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"DNA Repair","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genetic Therapy","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Editing","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["H