, MO, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Ramos-Espinosa O","lastName":"Ramos-Espinosa","firstName":"Octavio","initials":"O","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Infectious Diseases, Allergy and Immunology, Department of Internal Medicine, Saint Louis University School of Medicine, Saint Louis, MO, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"de Lima DS","lastName":"de Lima","firstName":"Dhemerson Souza","initials":"DS","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Infectious Diseases, Allergy and Immunology, Department of Internal Medicine, Saint Louis University School of Medicine, Saint Louis, MO, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Liu EY","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Ethan Y","initials":"EY","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Arts and Sciences; Saint Louis University, Saint Louis, MO, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Vaidyan S","lastName":"Vaidyan","firstName":"Sarah","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Arts and Sciences; Saint Louis University, Saint Louis, MO, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Liu J","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Jianguo","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Infectious Diseases, Allergy and Immunology, Department of Internal Medicine, Saint Louis University School of Medicine, Saint Louis, MO, USA."},{"affiliation":"Department of Molecular Microbiology and Immunology, Saint Louis University School of Medicine, Saint Louis, MO, USA."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8239-504X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1040-627X"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"8","volume":"16","journalIssueId":4184635,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Apr","monthOfPublication":4,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Bio Protoc","title":"Bio-protocol","essn":"2331-8325","issn":"2331-8325","isoabbreviation":"Bio Protoc","nlmid":"101635102"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-04-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e5660","abstractText":"We established a step-by-step approach for generating a single-nucleotide mutation in the promoter region of an immune regulatory gene in human monocyte THP-1 cells by employing a plasmid-based CRISPR-Cas9 system delivered via transfection with a homology-directed repair template DNA (HDR). Key steps include designing a single-guide RNA (sgRNA), cloning it into a CRISPR plasmid encoding the Cas9 protein, transfection of the plasmid constructs along with single-stranded oligonucleotide repair template (ssODNs) into THP-1 cells, followed by selection and validation. This approach provides a precise and relevant model to investigate the role of single polymorphisms in the regulation of inflammatory gene expression in human monocytes. In addition to the rs1024611 single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNP), this CRISPR/Cas9-based strategy is broadly applicable to functional studies of noncoding and coding variants in innate immune genes. Key features • Precise genome editing: CRISPR-Cas9-mediated editing of the rs1024611 SNP in the endogenous <i>CCL2</i> promoter in THP-1 cells using a single-stranded donor oligonucleotide. • Generate THP-1 monocytic cell lines: Differing only at the rs1024611 locus, allowing precise comparison of allele-specific effects on the same genetic background. • The protocol includes strategies for single-cell cloning, PCR-based genotyping, and Sanger sequencing to confirm precise genome editing. • While this study focuses on the <i>CCL2</i>-2518 SNP, it provides a framework for future investigations of other noncoding variants or regulatory SNPs in immune-related genes.","affiliation":"Division of Infectious Diseases, Allergy and Immunology, Department of Internal Medicine, Saint Louis University School of Medicine, Saint Louis, MO, USA.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic-eCollection","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["methods-article","Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["THP-1 cells","Single-nucleotide polymorphism","Crispr-cas9","Rs1024611 Snp","Single-Cell Clonal Isolation"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.21769/BioProtoc.5660"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13103971"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13103971?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by-nc","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["refsnp","doi"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-04-27","dateOfCreation":"2026-04-27","dateOfRevision":"2026-08-13","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-04-20","firstPublicationDate":"2026-04-20","firstIndexDate":"2026-04-27","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-04-24","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"41762386","source":"MED","pmid":"41762386","pmcid":"PMC12950078","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC12950078"]},"doi":"10.1007/s12026-026-09758-2","title":"CRISPR-Cas9-based gene editing as a proof-of-concept approach in an inborn error of immunity caused by a DCLRE1C variant.","authorString":"Duran T, Karaselek MA, Dagdelen B, Kuccukturk S, Guner SN, Keles S, Reisli I.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Duran T","lastName":"Duran","firstName":"Tugce","initials":"T","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Medicine Faculty, Department of Medical Genetics, KTO Karatay University, Konya, Turkey."},{"affiliation":"Medicine Faculty, Department of Pediatric Immunology and Allergy, Necmettin Erbakan University, Konya, Turkey."}]}},{"fullName":"Karaselek MA","lastName":"Karaselek","firstName":"Mehmet Ali","initials":"MA","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3201-8945"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Medicine Faculty, Department of Pediatric Immunology and Allergy, Necmettin Erbakan University, Konya, Turkey. malikaraselek@gmail.com."}]}},{"fullName":"Dagdelen B","lastName":"Dagdelen","firstName":"Burak","initials":"B","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4362-3852"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Medicine Faculty, Department of Medical Biology, Selcuk University, Konya, Turkey."}]}},{"fullName":"Kuccukturk S","lastName":"Kuccukturk","firstName":"Serkan","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8445-666X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Medicine Faculty, Department of Medical Biology, Karamanoğlu Mehmetbey University, Karaman, Turkey."}]}},{"fullName":"Guner SN","lastName":"Guner","firstName":"Sükrü Nail","initials":"SN","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Medicine Faculty, Department of Pediatric Immunology and Allergy, Necmettin Erbakan University, Konya, Turkey."}]}},{"fullName":"Keles S","lastName":"Keles","firstName":"Sevgi","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Medicine Faculty, Department of Pediatric Immunology and Allergy, Necmettin Erbakan University, Konya, Turkey."}]}},{"fullName":"Reisli I","lastName":"Reisli","firstName":"Ismail","initials":"I","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Medicine Faculty, Department of Pediatric Immunology and Allergy, Necmettin Erbakan University, Konya, Turkey."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8445-666X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4362-3852"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3201-8945"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"74","journalIssueId":4118603,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Immunol Res","title":"Immunologic research","essn":"1559-0755","issn":"0257-277X","isoabbreviation":"Immunol Res","nlmid":"8611087"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-02-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"20","abstractText":"Hypomorphic DCLRE1C variants impair T and B cell development, leading to combined immunodeficiency (CID) or leaky severe combined immunodeficiency (SCID). Current treatment options, such as allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (aHSCT), are associated with significant risks, highlighting the need for alternative therapeutic strategies. In this study, we report the first a proof-of-concept CRISPR-Cas9–mediated correction of a hypomorphic DCLRE1C variant (c.194 C > T; p.T65I) in CD4 + helper T (Th) cells using CRISPR-Cas9 gene-editing technology. CD4 + Th cells were isolated, and the variant region was edited with sgRNA and donor DNA. Gene editing efficiency was confirmed by Sanger sequencing, revealing successful restoration of the target region to its wild-type sequence. Functional analyses showed a significant increase in CD25 activation and Artemis protein expression post-editing, although DCLRE1C mRNA levels remained unchanged. The approximately 6–8% increase in CD25 expression was statistically significant but did not reach healthy control levels. These findings suggest that CRISPR-Cas9 –mediated gene editing may enable precise correction and induce measurable cellular-level functional changes, supporting biological feasibility rather than therapeutic efficacy. This study provides a foundation for future research on HSCs and underscores the potential role of CRISPR-Cas9–based approaches in the treatment of inborn errors of immunity (IEIs) associated with DCLRE1C variants.","affiliation":"Medicine Faculty, Department of Medical Genetics, KTO Karatay University, Konya, Turkey.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Necmettin Erbakan University","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Severe Combined Immunodeficiency","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Endonucleases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"DNA-Binding Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Nuclear Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Interleukin-2 Receptor alpha Subunit","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Editing","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Gene therapy","Artemis","Crispr-cas9","Dclre1c"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Endonucleases","registryNumber":"EC 3.1.-"},{"name":"Nuclear Proteins","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"DNA-Binding Proteins","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Interleukin-2 Receptor alpha Subunit","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"DCLRE1C protein, human","registryNumber":"EC 3.1.-"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12026-026-09758-2"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC12950078"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC12950078?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":1,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["pdb","doi"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-06-27","dateOfCreation":"2026-02-28","dateOfRevision":"2026-08-13","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-02-28","firstPublicationDate":"2026-02-28","firstIndexDate":"2026-03-01","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-03-02","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"41837831","source":"MED","pmid":"41837831","pmcid":"PMC13374948","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13374948"]},"doi":"10.4103/aam.aam_864_25","title":"CRISPR-cas9-Mediated Gene Editing to Reverse Oncogenic Mutations in Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma.","authorString":"Awinashe M, Viswaja K, Pathath AW, Subair FP, Varshney A, Mishra P, Mulla M, Mulla M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Awinashe M","lastName":"Awinashe","firstName":"Minal","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Diagnostic Science, College of Dentistry, Qassim University, Qassim, Saudi Arabia."}]}},{"fullName":"Viswaja K","lastName":"Viswaja","firstName":"K","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of General Pathology, SRM Dental College, Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Pathath AW","lastName":"Pathath","firstName":"Abdul Wahab","initials":"AW","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3180-8892"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Clinical Neuroscience, College of Medicine, King Faisal University, Al Ahsa, Saudi Arabia."}]}},{"fullName":"Subair FP","lastName":"Subair","firstName":"Fahida P","initials":"FP","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Kuien's Total Oral Health Center, Malappuram, Kerala, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Varshney A","lastName":"Varshney","firstName":"Anchal","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Oral Patholgy and Microbiology, School of Dental Sciences, Manav Rachna Dental College, MRIIRS, Faridabad, Haryana, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Mishra P","lastName":"Mishra","firstName":"Pallavi","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Pathology, Kalinga Institute of Dental Sciences, KIIT Deemed to be University, Bhubaneswar, Odisha, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Mulla M","lastName":"Mulla","firstName":"Mushir","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Public Health, College of Applied Medical Sciences, Qassim University, Qassim, Saudi Arabia."}]}},{"fullName":"Mulla M","lastName":"Mulla","firstName":"Munaz","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Periodontics, Saveetha Dental College and Hospitals, Saveetha Institute of Medical and Technical Sciences, Saveetha University, Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3180-8892"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0007-0472-0151"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"4","volume":"25","journalIssueId":4217536,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Ann Afr Med","title":"Annals of African medicine","essn":"0975-5764","issn":"1596-3519","isoabbreviation":"Ann Afr Med","nlmid":"101231417"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-07-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"805-809","abstractText":"<h4>Introduction</h4>Oral squamous cell carcinoma (OSCC) is a genetically driven malignancy characterized by a high burden of oncogenic mutations that contribute to aggressive tumor behavior, therapeutic resistance, and poor survival outcomes. Conventional treatment modalities largely target downstream molecular pathways without correcting the underlying genetic aberrations, underscoring the need for precision-based therapeutic strategies. This study aimed to assess the feasibility and functional impact of CRISPR-Cas9-mediated gene editing in reversing oncogenic mutations associated with OSCC using an in vitro experimental model.<h4>Materials and methods</h4>A controlled in vitro experimental study was conducted using the established human OSCC cell lines harboring mutations in key oncogenic genes. Cells were divided into control, mock-transfected, and CRISPR-Cas9-edited groups. Target-specific single-guide RNAs were designed to correct oncogenic mutations using advanced CRISPR-based editing platforms. Gene-editing efficiency was validated by molecular assays, while functional outcomes were assessed using cell proliferation analysis. Statistical evaluation was done using the one-way ANOVA with significance set at P < 0.05.<h4>Results</h4>CRISPR-Cas9-edited OSCC cells demonstrated a significant reduction in cell proliferation compared to control and mock-transfected groups ( P < 0.001). No significant variation was found between control and mock-transfected cells, confirming minimal procedural influence.<h4>Conclusion</h4>CRISPR-Cas9-mediated correction of oncogenic mutations effectively suppresses malignant cellular proliferation in OSCC, highlighting its promising role as a precision therapeutic strategy in oral cancer management.","affiliation":"Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Diagnostic Science, College of Dentistry, Qassim University, Qassim, Saudi Arabia.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Line, Tumor"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Carcinoma, Squamous Cell","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Mouth Neoplasms","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Proliferation","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Mutation"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Oncogenes"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Editing","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma","Molecular Therapy","Gene Editing","Crispr-cas9","Precision Oncology","Édition Génique","Carcinome Épidermoïde Oral","Inversion De Mutation Oncogène","Oncogenic Mutation Reversal","Thérapie Moléculaire","Oncologie De Précision"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.4103/aam.aam_864_25"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13374948"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13374948?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","license":"cc by-nc-nd","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2026-06-15","dateOfCreation":"2026-03-16","dateOfRevision":"2026-08-13","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-03-16","firstPublicationDate":"2026-03-16","firstIndexDate":"2026-03-17","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-09-03","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42922986","source":"MED","pmid":"42922986","pmcid":"PMC13687265","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13687265"]},"doi":"10.3389/fpls.2026.1927332","title":"CRISPR/Cas9-mediated editing of &lt;i&gt;SlALS1&lt;/i&gt; enhances fruit sweetness in tomato.","authorString":"Yang SH, Han SK, Koo Y.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Yang SH","lastName":"Yang","firstName":"So Hee","initials":"SH","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Agricultural Chemistry, Chonnam National University, Gwangju, Republic of Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Han SK","lastName":"Han","firstName":"Soon-Ki","initials":"SK","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Ajou University, Suwon, Republic of Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Koo Y","lastName":"Koo","firstName":"Yeonjong","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Agricultural Chemistry, Chonnam National University, Gwangju, Republic of Korea."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Environmentally-friendly Agriculture, Chonnam National University, Gwangju, Republic of Korea."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Plant Biomaterials and Biomedical Science, Chonnam National University, Gwangju, Republic of Korea."}]}}]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"17","journalIssueId":4112080,"dateOfPublication":"2026 ","monthOfPublication":0,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Front Plant Sci","title":"Frontiers in plant science","essn":"1664-462X","issn":"1664-462X","isoabbreviation":"Front Plant Sci","nlmid":"101568200"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-01-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"1927332","abstractText":"Fruit sweetness is a primary determinant of consumer preference and market value in tomato (<i>Solanum lycopersicum</i>), yet increasing sugar content without negatively affecting plant performance remains a major challenge in breeding programs. In this study, we targeted <i>Acetolactate synthase 1</i> (<i>SlALS1</i>), a key enzyme in branched-chain amino acids (BCAAs) biosynthesis, to investigate whether modulation of primary metabolism could enhance fruit sugar accumulation. Tomato contains two ALS homologs, <i>SlALS1</i> and <i>SlALS2</i>. Using CRISPR/Cas9-mediated genome editing, we generated <i>SlALS1</i> knock-out lines in the Micro-Tom background. Loss of <i>SlALS1</i> function led to a significant reduction in the levels of valine, leucine, and isoleucine in fruit tissues, confirming disruption of the BCAA biosynthetic pathway. Notably, soluble sugar content was markedly increased in the mutant lines, with glucose and fructose levels elevated by approximately 1.3-fold compared with wild-type fruits, resulting in a significantly higher Brix index. Metabolic profiling indicates that reduced BCAA biosynthesis may influence carbon allocation toward soluble sugar accumulation in fruit tissues, revealing an association between amino acid metabolism and carbohydrate accumulation during fruit development. Our findings demonstrate that precise editing of a central metabolic enzyme can enhance tomato fruit sweetness and suggest that <i>SlALS1</i> may represent a promising target for genome editing aimed at improving fruit quality traits. However, further evaluation of agronomic traits, including plant growth and fruit yield, will be necessary to assess its potential for practical breeding applications.","affiliation":"Department of Agricultural Chemistry, Chonnam National University, Gwangju, Republic of Korea.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic-eCollection","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Tomato","branched-chain amino acid biosynthesis","Solanum Lycopersicum","Crispr/cas9","Fruit Sweetness","Precision Breeding","Soluble Sugar Accumulation","Acetolactate Synthase 1 (Slals1)"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpls.2026.1927332"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13687265"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13687265?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2026-10-24","dateOfCreation":"2026-10-24","dateOfRevision":"2026-10-25","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-10-0