versity, Samutprakarn, 10540, Thailand."}]}},{"fullName":"Phanthong P","lastName":"Phanthong","firstName":"Phetcharat","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Anatomy, Faculty of Science, Mahidol University, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand."}]}},{"fullName":"Borwornpinyo S","lastName":"Borwornpinyo","firstName":"Suparerk","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6211-3615"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biotechnology, Faculty of Science, Mahidol University, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand."},{"affiliation":"Excellence Center for Drug Discovery, Faculty of Science, Mahidol University, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand."}]}},{"fullName":"Chiangjong W","lastName":"Chiangjong","firstName":"Wararat","initials":"W","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Pediatric Translational Research Unit, Department of Pediatrics, Faculty of Medicine Ramathibodi Hospital, Mahidol University, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand."}]}},{"fullName":"Sa-Ngiamsuntorn K","lastName":"Sa-Ngiamsuntorn","firstName":"Khanit","initials":"K","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7010-345X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry, Faculty of Pharmacy, Mahidol University, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand."},{"affiliation":"Biomarker and Epigenetic Science for Targeted Therapeutics (BEST) Research Center, Faculty of Pharmacy, Mahidol University, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand."}]}},{"fullName":"Hongeng S","lastName":"Hongeng","firstName":"Suradej","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Pediatrics, Faculty of Medicine Ramathibodi Hospital, Mahidol University, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6211-3615"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7010-345X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2267-7883"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"51","journalIssueId":4212146,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Biotechnol Rep (Amst)","title":"Biotechnology reports (Amsterdam, Netherlands)","essn":"2215-017X","issn":"2215-017X","isoabbreviation":"Biotechnol Rep (Amst)","nlmid":"101637426"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-09-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e00961","abstractText":"Chronic hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection remains a major global health burden due to the persistence of covalently closed circular DNA (cccDNA), which limits current antiviral therapies. We developed an adeno-associated virus (AAV)-delivered CRISPR/Cas9 system targeting conserved regions of the HBV genome. Three guide RNAs (gRNA1-3) targeting overlapping open reading frames of the surface antigen and polymerase genes were evaluated in HepG2.2.15 cells and HBV-infected hepatocyte-like cells (imHCs), with a reverse transcriptase-targeting gRNA and tenofovir alafenamide as controls. All gRNAs significantly reduced intracellular and extracellular HBV DNA levels and moderately decreased HBsAg secretion. Notably, gRNA2 induced a frameshift mutation and demonstrated superior antiviral efficacy, markedly reducing cccDNA levels, viral DNA levels, viral RNA levels, HBcAg expression, and HBsAg secretion with suppression maintained for up to 12 days. These findings highlight AAV-mediated CRISPR/Cas9 as a promising gene-based therapy for chronic HBV infection.","affiliation":"Department of Biotechnology, Faculty of Science, Mahidol University, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic-eCollection","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["HBV","Hepatocytes","AAV","Cccdna","Crispr/cas9","Guide Rna","Imhc"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.btre.2026.e00961"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13234202"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13234202?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["gen","pdb","doi"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-06-08","dateOfCreation":"2026-06-08","dateOfRevision":"2026-08-13","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-05-19","firstPublicationDate":"2026-05-19","firstIndexDate":"2026-06-09","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-06-07","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42458955","source":"MED","pmid":"42458955","pmcid":"PMC13373454","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13373454"]},"doi":"10.1111/mpp.70312","title":"Enhanced Rice Yellow Mottle Virus Resistance via CRISPR/Cas9-Targeted Mutagenesis of the Rice eIF(iso)4G Gene.","authorString":"Kigaru A, Ateka EM, Pappu HR, Nganga EM, Murori R, Toili ME, Runo S.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Kigaru A","lastName":"Kigaru","firstName":"Antony","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1826-7777"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Molecular Biology and Biotechnology, Pan African University Institute for Basic Sciences, Technology and Innovation, Nairobi, Kenya."},{"affiliation":"Department of Crop Sciences, Bukura Agricultural College, Kakamega, Kenya."}]}},{"fullName":"Ateka EM","lastName":"Ateka","firstName":"Elijah M","initials":"EM","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Horticulture and Food Security, Jomo Kenyatta University of Agriculture and Technology, Nairobi, Kenya."},{"affiliation":"Department of Plant, Animal and Food Sciences, Jaramogi Odinga Oginga University of Science and Technology, Bondo, Kenya."}]}},{"fullName":"Pappu HR","lastName":"Pappu","firstName":"Hanu R","initials":"HR","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Plant Pathology, Washington State University, Pullman, Washington, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Nganga EM","lastName":"Nganga","firstName":"Everlyne M","initials":"EM","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"International Rice Research Institute, Nairobi, Kenya."}]}},{"fullName":"Murori R","lastName":"Murori","firstName":"Rosemary","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"International Rice Research Institute, Nairobi, Kenya."}]}},{"fullName":"Toili ME","lastName":"Toili","firstName":"Mary Esther","initials":"ME","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry, Microbiology and Biotechnology, Kenyatta University, Nairobi, Kenya."}]}},{"fullName":"Runo S","lastName":"Runo","firstName":"Steven","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9043-2338"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Molecular Biology and Biotechnology, Pan African University Institute for Basic Sciences, Technology and Innovation, Nairobi, Kenya."},{"affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry, Microbiology and Biotechnology, Kenyatta University, Nairobi, Kenya."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6311-8394"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9043-2338"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1826-7777"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"7","volume":"27","journalIssueId":4222033,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Mol Plant Pathol","title":"Molecular plant pathology","essn":"1364-3703","issn":"1364-3703","isoabbreviation":"Mol Plant Pathol","nlmid":"100954969"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-07-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e70312","abstractText":"Rice is a staple crop primarily recognised for its high content of carbohydrates and proteins. Rice yellow mottle disease (RYMD) is a destructive disease affecting rice fields in sub-Saharan Africa and is caused by the rice yellow mottle virus (RYMV). Development of virus-resistant genotypes is a highly recommended and effective approach to controlling RYMV. A genetic approach that exploits recessive mutations in susceptibility (S) genes may enhance resistance to the virus. Reports indicate that most rice genotypes grown in Kenya are vulnerable to RYMV infection. Genome editing has shown promise in enhancing agronomic traits in crops. We obtained enhanced resistance to RYMV in the Indica rice cv. IR2793-80-01 using the CRISPR-Cas9 system. The eIF(iso)4G susceptibility gene was targeted because natural mutations in this gene confer recessive resistance to RYMV. A Cas9-OseIF(iso)4G-gRNA-expressing vector targeting the eIF(iso)4G gene was introduced into rice calli via Agrobacterium-mediated transformation. Ten T<sub>2</sub> homozygous mutant plant lines were assessed for their reaction to RYMV, and infection was significantly reduced. There were no significant differences in the agronomic characteristics between the T<sub>2</sub> mutant lines and the wild-type plants. CRISPR/Cas9-mediated knockout alleles of the eIF(iso)4G gene conferred enhanced resistance to RYMV, which may be classified as partial. Findings underscore the need to embrace precise editing strategies, such as prime editing, to generate superior resistance alleles. Overall, the study provides an alternative resistance enhancement strategy that can create knockout resistance alleles that can be incorporated into breeding programmes for RYMV resistance.","affiliation":"Department of Molecular Biology and Biotechnology, Pan African University Institute for Basic Sciences, Technology and Innovation, Nairobi, Kenya.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"African Union Commission","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Plant Viruses","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PY","qualifierName":"pathogenicity"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Plants, Genetically Modified"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Plant Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Eukaryotic Initiation Factor-4G","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Plant Diseases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"VI","qualifierName":"virology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Mutagenesis","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mutation","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Genes, Plant"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Disease Resistance","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{